le at: http://www.oregon.gov/DHS/ph/genetics/plan.shtml . Accessed January 11, 2006. 26. Rhode Island Department of Health. Rhode Island State genetics plan. 2002. Available at: http://genes-r-us.uthscsa.edu/resources/genetics/rhodeisland_geneticsplan.pdf . Accessed January 11, 2006. 27. Maternal and Child Health, Genetics and NBS, Tennessee Department of Health. Tennessee genetics plan. 2003. Available at: http://www2.state.tn.us/health/Downloads/Genetics_Plan_2003.pdf . Accessed January 11, 2006. 28. Genetics Program, Texas Department of State Health Services. The development of the Texas State genetics plan and a plan for integrated data infrastructure for genetic services. 2002. Available at: http://genes-r-us.uthscsa.edu/resources/genetics/texas_geneticsplan.pdf . Accessed January 11, 2006. 29. Children with Special Health Care Needs, Division of Community and Family Health Services, Utah Department of Health. Utah State genetics plan. 2002. Available at: http://genes-r-us.uthscsa.edu/resources/genetics/utah_geneticsplan.pdf . Accessed January 11, 2006. 30. Washington State Department of Health. Genetic services section plan. 2002–2005. Available at: http://mchneighborhood.ichp.edu/wagenetics/index.html . Accessed January 27, 2006. 31. Genetic services plan for Wisconsin. Available at: http://www.slh.wisc.edu/genetics . Accessed January 11, 2006. 32. Reynolds PP, Kamei RK, Sundquist J, Khanna N, Palmer EJ, Palmer T. Using the PRACTICE mnemonic to apply cultural competency to genetics in medical education and patient care. Acad Med. 2005;80:1107–1113. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 33. Bernhardt JM, McClain J, Parrott RL. Online health communication about human genetics: perceptions and preferences of internet users. Cyberpsychol Behav. 2004;7:728–733. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 34. Sanderson SC, Wardle J. Will genetic testing for complex diseases increase motivation to quit smoking? Anticipated reactions in a survey of smokers. Health Educ Beh